   <p>To his Excellincy Governor, <persName ref="cwgk:N001000">Tho<hi rend="sup">s</hi>. E. Bramlett</persName>,</p>
<p>The undersigned petitioners say that <persName ref="cwgk:N00014313">S. W. Clark</persName> is a citizen of <placeName ref="cwgk:P00000544">Pendleton County</placeName> and our neighbors; We know him to be a good citizen and a law abiding man, We also think &amp; believe that the prosecution in this case against him was prompted by personal anemosity &amp; not for the peace and quiet &amp; the good morals of his immediate neighborhood. We recommend him to your clemency, <date when="1865-04-26">April 26<hi rend="sup">th</hi> 1865.</date> The prosecution is for keeping a tippling house and the fine assessed at the present <date when="1865-04">April Term</date> of the <orgName ref="cwgk:O00000489">Pendleton Circuit Court</orgName> is sixty dollars, which we think ought to be remitted</p>
<p><milestone unit="column" n="2"/><cb n="1"/><persName ref="cwgk:N00014314">G B, Parker</persName>
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N00014315">George. W. Booker</persName>
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N00014316">W<hi rend="sup">m</hi> G. P Weaver</persName>
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N00003659">D. N. Williams</persName>
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N00014317">John Douglass</persName>
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N00014318">Squire Jett</persName>
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N00014319">F, M, Aulich</persName>
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N00014320">S C, Edwards</persName>
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N00014321">J. C, Garrard</persName>
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N00014244">N. C. Wilson</persName>
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N00014322">G. M. Calvin</persName>
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N00010828">James Wilson</persName>
<lb/><cb n="2"/><persName ref="cwgk:N00014323">C. C. Aulich</persName>
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N00014324">Robert Purdy</persName>
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N00010825">W<hi rend="sup">m</hi> <hi rend="underline">M</hi><hi rend="underline"><hi rend="sup">c</hi></hi><hi rend="underline">Murchy</hi></persName>
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N00010837">J. T Applegate</persName>
